---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
    title="Word Counter — Free Online Word & Character Counter"
    description="Free online word counter. Count words, characters, sentences, and paragraphs instantly. Estimate reading time. No signup required."
>
    <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold mb-3">Word Counter</h1>
        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-6">
            Paste or type your text below to instantly count words, characters,
            sentences, and reading time.
        </p>

        <textarea
            id="text-input"
            class="w-full h-64 p-4 border border-gray-300 rounded-lg focus:outline-none focus:ring-2 focus:ring-blue-500 resize-y"
            placeholder="Type or paste your text here..."></textarea>

        <div class="flex gap-3 mt-3">
            <button
                id="copy-btn"
                class="px-4 py-2 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700 text-sm font-medium"
            >
                Copy Text
            </button>
            <button
                id="clear-btn"
                class="px-4 py-2 bg-gray-200 text-gray-800 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-300 text-sm font-medium"
            >
                Clear
            </button>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-2 md:grid-cols-4 gap-4 mt-6">
            <div
                class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 text-center"
            >
                <div id="word-count" class="text-3xl font-bold text-blue-600">
                    0
                </div>
                <div class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Words</div>
            </div>
            <div
                class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 text-center"
            >
                <div id="char-count" class="text-3xl font-bold text-blue-600">
                    0
                </div>
                <div class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Characters</div>
            </div>
            <div
                class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 text-center"
            >
                <div
                    id="sentence-count"
                    class="text-3xl font-bold text-blue-600"
                >
                    0
                </div>
                <div class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Sentences</div>
            </div>
            <div
                class="bg-white p-4 rounded-lg border border-gray-200 text-center"
            >
                <div id="reading-time" class="text-3xl font-bold text-blue-600">
                    0m
                </div>
                <div class="text-sm text-gray-600 mt-1">Reading Time</div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    <!-- SEO Content (800+ words) -->
    <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-16 prose prose-gray">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">About This Word Counter</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            This free online word counter instantly counts words, characters,
            sentences, and estimates reading time. It's perfect for students
            checking essay limits, bloggers hitting SEO targets, social media
            managers staying within platform limits, and anyone who needs an
            accurate count without opening a heavy word processor.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Unlike most word counters that require an account or send your text
            to a server, this tool runs entirely in your browser. Your text
            never leaves your device. Paste something confidential — a client
            contract, a personal essay, a private message — and it stays
            private.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">How to Use</h3>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>Paste or type your text into the box above.</li>
            <li>Word, character, and sentence counts update in real time.</li>
            <li>
                Use the "Copy Text" button to copy your text, or "Clear" to
                start over.
            </li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">Why Use This Tool?</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>
                <strong>Real-time counting:</strong> Numbers update as you type —
                no need to click a button.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Multiple metrics at once:</strong> Words, characters, sentences,
                and reading time in one view.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Privacy first:</strong> Everything runs in your browser. No
                uploads, no tracking.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Free with no limits:</strong> Count as many texts as you want,
                as often as you want.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Works on any device:</strong> Desktop, laptop, tablet, or
                phone — no app needed.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">Common Use Cases</h3>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">1. Checking Essay Word Limits</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Most academic essays have strict word limits — 500, 1,000, 1,500, or
            5,000 words depending on the level. Paste your draft here and see
            exactly where you stand. No more submitting a 1,453-word essay when
            the requirement was 1,500.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">
            2. Hitting SEO Targets for Blog Posts
        </h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            SEO-friendly blog posts are typically 1,000–2,000 words. Paste your
            draft here to check your count before publishing. If you're short,
            add examples or a FAQ section; if you're long, trim redundant
            sentences.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">
            3. Staying Within Social Media Limits
        </h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Twitter/X has a 280-character limit. Instagram captions cap at 2,200
            characters. LinkedIn posts perform best under 1,300 characters.
            Paste your caption here to avoid the dreaded "too long" warning.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">4. Writing Meta Descriptions</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Google truncates meta descriptions after about 155 characters. Paste
            your draft here and check the character count before adding it to
            your page's `<head>`. </head>

            <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">
                5. Preparing Product Descriptions
            </h4>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
                E-commerce platforms often have character limits for product
                titles (60–70) and descriptions (150–300). This tool makes it
                easy to stay within bounds.
            </p>

            <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">
                6. Checking Reading Time for Articles
            </h4>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
                Reading time estimates help set expectations for readers. A
                1,000-word article takes about 5 minutes to read at 200 words
                per minute. This tool shows that automatically.
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">A Worked Example</h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
                Here's what happens when you paste this paragraph:
            </p>
            <pre
                class="bg-gray-100 p-4 rounded-lg text-sm overflow-x-auto mb-4"><code>Word counting is one of those small skills that saves real time. Whether you're writing a 2,000-word blog post or a 280-character tweet, getting the count right matters.</code></pre>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">The tool shows:</p>
            <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
                <li><strong>Words:</strong> 29</li>
                <li><strong>Characters:</strong> 172 (including spaces)</li>
                <li><strong>Sentences:</strong> 2</li>
                <li><strong>Reading time:</strong> 1 minute</li>
            </ul>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4 mb-4">
                That's the exact information you need — without opening Word,
                Google Docs, or any other app.
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">
                How Reading Time Is Calculated
            </h3>
            <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
                This tool uses an average adult reading speed of <strong
                    >200 words per minute</strong
                >. That's the standard used by most reading-time calculators,
                including those on major publishing platforms. Technical or
                academic content may take longer — closer to 150 WPM — while
                fiction reads faster at around 250 WPM.
            </p>

            <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">
                Frequently Asked Questions
            </h3>
            <div class="space-y-4 mt-3">
                <div>
                    <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        Is my text saved anywhere?
                    </h4>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        No. All counting happens in your browser. Your text
                        never leaves your device, and nothing is stored on any
                        server.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        How is reading time calculated?
                    </h4>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        Reading time is estimated at 200 words per minute, which
                        is the average adult reading speed. A 1,000-word article
                        shows as 5 minutes.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        Does this count characters with or without spaces?
                    </h4>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        The character count includes spaces, punctuation, and
                        line breaks — everything that makes up the text length.
                        This matches how social media platforms and form
                        validators count characters.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        How are sentences counted?
                    </h4>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        Sentences are detected by periods, exclamation marks,
                        and question marks. Abbreviations like "Dr." may add
                        extra counts — this is a limitation of any
                        sentence-counting tool.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        Can I count words in a specific section only?
                    </h4>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        Yes. Highlight just the section you want to count, then
                        paste it into the tool. The count will reflect only that
                        selection.
                    </p>
                </div>
                <div>
                    <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">
                        Is this tool free?
                    </h4>
                    <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">
                        Yes, completely free with no limits or signup. Use it as
                        often as you need.
                    </p>
                </div>
            </div>
        </p>

        <!-- Related Tools & Guides -->
        <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-16">
            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Related Tools</h2>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4 mb-10">
                <a
                    href="/tools/json-formatter/"
                    class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
                >
                    <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">JSON Formatter</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                        Format and validate JSON data.
                    </p>
                </a>
                <a
                    href="/tools/qr-generator/"
                    class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
                >
                    <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">QR Code Generator</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                        Create custom QR codes for any URL.
                    </p>
                </a>
                <a
                    href="/tools/password-generator/"
                    class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
                >
                    <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Password Generator</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                        Create strong, random passwords.
                    </p>
                </a>
            </div>

            <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Related Guides</h2>
            <div class="space-y-3">
                <a
                    href="/blog/how-to-count-words/"
                    class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
                >
                    <h3 class="font-medium">How to Count Words Accurately</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                        Complete guide for essays, blogs, and social media.
                    </p>
                </a>
                <a
                    href="/blog/word-count-google-docs-all-tabs/"
                    class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
                >
                    <h3 class="font-medium">
                        How to Count Words Across All Tabs in Google Docs
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                        Multiple tabs ka total count.
                    </p>
                </a>
                <a
                    href="/blog/twitter-character-count/"
                    class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
                >
                    <h3 class="font-medium">Twitter/X Character Count Guide</h3>
                    <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                        Stay within the 280-character limit.
                    </p>
                </a>
            </div>
        </section>

        <script>
            const input = document.getElementById(
                "text-input",
            ) as HTMLTextAreaElement;
            const wordCount = document.getElementById("word-count")!;
            const charCount = document.getElementById("char-count")!;
            const sentenceCount = document.getElementById("sentence-count")!;
            const readingTime = document.getElementById("reading-time")!;

            function updateCounts() {
                const text = input.value;

                const words = text.trim() ? text.trim().split(/\s+/).length : 0;
                const chars = text.length;
                const sentences = text.trim()
                    ? text.split(/[.!?]+/).filter((s) => s.trim().length > 0)
                          .length
                    : 0;
                const minutes = Math.ceil(words / 200);

                wordCount.textContent = words.toString();
                charCount.textContent = chars.toString();
                sentenceCount.textContent = sentences.toString();
                readingTime.textContent = minutes + "m";
            }

            input.addEventListener("input", updateCounts);

            document
                .getElementById("copy-btn")!
                .addEventListener("click", () => {
                    if (input.value) {
                        navigator.clipboard.writeText(input.value);
                    }
                });

            document
                .getElementById("clear-btn")!
                .addEventListener("click", () => {
                    input.value = "";
                    updateCounts();
                    input.focus();
                });
        </script>

        <script
            type="application/ld+json"
            set:html={JSON.stringify({
                "@context": "https://schema.org",
                "@type": "SoftwareApplication",
                name: "Word Counter",
                applicationCategory: "UtilityApplication",
                operatingSystem: "Any",
                description:
                    "Free online word counter. Count words, characters, sentences, and estimate reading time instantly.",
                offers: {
                    "@type": "Offer",
                    price: "0",
                    priceCurrency: "USD",
                },
            })}
        />

        <!-- FAQPage Schema -->
        <script
            type="application/ld+json"
            set:html={JSON.stringify({
                "@context": "https://schema.org",
                "@type": "FAQPage",
                mainEntity: [
                    {
                        "@type": "Question",
                        name: "Is my text saved anywhere?",
                        acceptedAnswer: {
                            "@type": "Answer",
                            text: "No. All counting happens in your browser. Your text never leaves your device.",
                        },
                    },
                    {
                        "@type": "Question",
                        name: "How is reading time calculated?",
                        acceptedAnswer: {
                            "@type": "Answer",
                            text: "Reading time is estimated at 200 words per minute, which is the average adult reading speed.",
                        },
                    },
                    {
                        "@type": "Question",
                        name: "Is this tool free?",
                        acceptedAnswer: {
                            "@type": "Answer",
                            text: "Yes, completely free with no limits or signup.",
                        },
                    },
                ],
            })}
        />
    </section>
</Layout>
